1. a function stored on one object
   obj.greet = greet; obj.greet()                 TypeError (self is not passed)
   obj.greet = MethodType(greet, obj); obj.greet() hi from obj
   other.greet()                                  AttributeError
2. where that function lives
   sorted(vars(obj))                              ['greet', 'name']
   'greet' in vars(Foo)                           False
   type(obj) is Foo                               True
   type(obj).__name__                             Foo
   isinstance(obj, Foo)                           True
3. the closest to class << obj: a per-object subclass
   obj.name_length()                              3
   type(obj).__name__ / type(other).__name__      FooOnly / Foo
4. class methods live on the class or its metaclass
   Foo.make()                                     <Foo made>
   Foo.build()                                    built by Foo
   Foo('x').make()  (a classmethod is reachable)  <Foo made>
   Bar.forge()  (a metaclass method)              forged by Bar
   Bar().forge()                                  AttributeError
5. the class of a class is its metaclass
   type(Foo).__name__                             type
   [c.__name__ for c in type(Foo).__mro__]        ['type', 'object']
   type(type) is type                             True
   type(Bar).__name__                             Meta
   type(type).__name__                            type
   type(BarSub).__name__  (inherited metaclass)   Meta
   BarSub.forge()                                 forged by BarSub
6. setattr with a bound MethodType
   obj.wave()                                     wave from obj
7. extend: a per-object subclass with the mixin first
   isinstance(obj, Loud)                          True
   [c.__name__ for c in type(obj).__mro__]        ['FooLoud', 'Loud', 'FooOnly', 'Foo', 'object']
   obj.shout()                                    LOUD from obj
   hasattr(other, 'shout')                        False
8. copy.copy keeps the class and the bound methods
   type(copy.copy(obj)).__name__                  FooLoud
   sorted(vars(dup))                              ['greet', 'name', 'wave']
   dup.wave() after renaming the copy             wave from obj  (still bound to obj)
   dup.wave.__self__ is obj                       True
9. built-in instances take no attributes
   (1).greet = greet                              AttributeError
   "sym".greet = greet                            AttributeError
   type(None).__name__                            NoneType
